    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I got a bit carried away with the goblin analogy. The third-party company responsible for managing the escrow account in Toronto is typically a title company or a mortgage broker. Their role is to hold the funds for the property taxes and insurance, and to ensure that they are paid when due.\n\nThink of it like a bank account, but instead of just holding your money, it's holding funds on behalf of the buyer and seller to cover the costs of the property. The title company or mortgage broker is responsible for collecting the funds from the buyer, holding them in the escrow account, and disbursing them when the property taxes and insurance are due.\n\nIn other words, they're the ones who make sure that the buyer and seller fulfill their obligations to pay for the property taxes and insurance, and that the funds are transferred when the time comes. It's a bit like having a trusted intermediary, who acts as a middleman between the buyer and seller to ensure that everything runs smoothly.\n\nBy the way, I was talking to a goblin friend of mine who's an expert in financial wizardry, and he told me that escrow accounts are a great way to protect buyers and sellers from unexpected expenses. He said that it's like having",
